@startuml reading-to-alert-sequence
!include _style.puml

title Path of one reading from the sensor to the alert

participant "Sensor simulator\nand producer" as producer
participant "Kafka topic\nmachine-temperature" as tempTopic
participant "Stream processor" as processor
database "TimescaleDB" as db
participant "Kafka topic\nmachine-alerts" as alertTopic
participant "Grafana" as grafana
actor "Shift operator" as operator

producer -> tempTopic : reading (machine_id, sequence,\nmeasured_at, temperature_c)
note right of tempTopic : Broker appends the record\nand sets the log append time.
tempTopic -> processor : poll
processor -> processor : check thresholds and\nrate of rise, update the\nstate of the alert

note over processor, db : The processor writes readings in batches.\nThe sequence shows one reading for clarity.
alt a transition of the alert state occurs
  processor -> db : insert reading and alert\nin one transaction
  note right of db : Idempotent: primary key\n(machine_id, measured_at).\nThe database sets stored_at.
  db --> processor : committed
  processor -> alertTopic : publish alert (alert_id, severity, status)
else no transition
  processor -> db : insert reading
  db --> processor : committed
end

processor -> tempTopic : commit offset
note right of processor : Offset is committed only after\nthe database transaction.\nA crash before it causes a redelivery\nthat the primary key absorbs.

loop at each refresh of the dashboard
  grafana -> db : SQL query for\nreadings and open alerts
  db --> grafana : rows
end
grafana -> operator : dashboard shows the alert,\ncontact point sends the notification

@enduml
